      "desc": "Veterinary care for dogs.",
      "narrative": "The current program of veterinary care for the eight, wolf-dog hybrids includes preventative treatment for parasites and\nother pests but does not include a schedule for sampling to monitor for these parasites (including fleas, worms, coccidia,\ngiardia, and heartworm). Failure to perform parasite sampling according to an attending veterinarian\u2019s approved schedule\ndoes not ensure the dogs are adequately protected from diseases and parasites. The licensee must ensure that\nvaccinations for contagious and/or deadly diseases of dogs (including rabies, parvovirus, and distemper) and sampling\nand treatment of parasites and other pests (including fleas, worms, coccidia, giardia, and heartworm) are followed in\naccordance with a schedule approved by the attending veterinarian.\nThis inspection and exit interview were conducted with a facility representative.\nn"
    }
